  m_text: "<align=\"center\"><size=150%><b>ManningCast Mayhem</b>\n<b>Terms and Conditions</b></size></align>\r\n\r\nThese
    terms govern access to and use of the ManningCast Mayhem online game, including
    its optional prize competition, optional high-score publicity, and optional marketing
    communications.\r\n\r\nThese terms are the complete agreement between you and
    <b>Omaha Productions LLC (\"Omaha\")</b> concerning the game and the optional
    activities mentioned above. There are no separate competition rules or privacy
    notice. All competition requirements and disclosures about the information collected
    through the game are contained in these terms.\r\n\r\nOmaha located at 11601
    Wilshire Boulevard, Los Angeles, CA 90025 operates the game. In these terms,
    \"we,\" \"us,\" and \"our\" refer to that company.\r\n\r\nBy accessing or using
    the game, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the game.
    If you enter the prize competition or select an optional consent, the additional
    provisions governing that activity also apply.\r\n\r\nNo purchase is necessary.
    You do not need an account or personal information to play. Entering the prize
    competition is optional and is limited to eligible adults in the United States.\r\n\r\n<b>1.
    No account is required</b>\r\nYou may play without creating an account, choosing
    a username or password, or submitting your name or email address.\r\n\r\nYou
    may also play without:\r\nentering the prize competition;\r\nreceiving competition
    or marketing communications; or\r\nauthorizing us to publicize your high score.\r\n\r\nThe
    game may process limited technical and gameplay information needed to operate
    and secure the game, calculate scores, and enforce these terms, as described
    in section 13.\r\n\r\n<b>2. Gameplay and optional activities are separate</b>\r\nThe
    following are separate choices:\r\nplaying the game without entering the prize
    competition;\r\nentering the prize competition by submitting the required entry
    information;\r\nchoosing whether we may publicize your high-score achievement;
    and\r\nchoosing whether to receive marketing communications.\r\n\r\nSubmitting
    information for one purpose does not enroll you in another purpose. A competition
    entry does not create an account or automatically enroll you in marketing or
    publicity.\r\n\r\n<b>3. Eligibility</b>\r\nYou may use the game only if your
    use is permitted where you live and you satisfy the applicable age requirements
    below.\r\n\r\nThe game is intended for a general audience and is not directed
    to children under 13. You must be at least 13 years old to use the game. A person
    under 13 may not use the game or submit information through it. If we learn that
    we collected personal information from a child under 13, we will delete it.\r\n\r\nIf
    you are 13 through 17, you may play only with the permission of your parent or
    legal guardian. You may not enter the prize competition, submit your name or
    email address, opt in to marketing communications, or authorize high-score publicity.\r\n\r\nYou
    must be at least 18 years old to enter the prize competition, submit a name or
    email address through the game, receive marketing communications, or authorize
    high-score publicity.\r\n\r\nThe game may be accessed from any location where
    it is available. Prize competition entry and prize eligibility are limited to
    legal residents of the United States who are at least 18 years old at the time
    of entry.\r\n\r\nEmployees, officers, directors, contractors, and immediate family
    or household members of the operator and its affiliates, and any other persons
    involved in developing, administering, or promoting the competition, are not
    eligible to enter or win.\r\n\r\n<b>4. Limited permission to use the game</b>\r\nSubject
    to these terms, we give you a limited, personal, revocable, nonexclusive, nontransferable
    right to access and use the game for lawful, noncommercial entertainment and,
    if eligible, to enter the prize competition.\r\n\r\nYou may not copy, modify,
    distribute, sell, sublicense, reverse engineer, interfere with, or use the game
    or its content except as these terms or applicable law expressly permit.\r\n\r\n<b>5.
    Ownership</b>\r\nThe game and its software, artwork, audiovisual material, text,
    designs, names, logos, and other content are owned by or licensed to us and are
    protected by intellectual-property laws. Except for the limited permission in
    section 4, these terms do not transfer any ownership or other rights to you.\r\n\r\nIf
    you voluntarily send us feedback about the game, you allow us to use it without
    restriction or compensation, but you do not transfer ownership of any personal
    information contained in the feedback.\r\n\r\n<b>6. Skill-based scoring</b>\r\nThe
    competition is intended to be a contest of skill. Winners are determined by verified
    game scores, not by a random drawing or other chance-based selection.\r\n\r\nEach
    play session begins with three lives. A player's score increases based on faster
    completion, the number of lives remaining at completion, and the point values
    associated with the spaces on which the player lands. Competition rankings are
    determined solely by verified scores produced by those gameplay factors.\r\n\r\nThe
    score displayed by the game at the end of a play session is the score used for
    competition ranking, subject to verification under section 7. The highest verified
    scores rank first.\r\n\r\n<b>7. Scores and verification</b>\r\nThe game may record
    a player's score, completion time, remaining lives, landing-space results, and
    other gameplay data needed to calculate and verify the score.\r\n\r\nWe may review
    entries and gameplay data to confirm eligibility, scoring accuracy, compliance
    with these terms, and fair play. We may correct an objectively documented scoring
    or technical error and may reject a score or entry produced through cheating,
    automation, tampering, exploitation of an unintended error, or other prohibited
    conduct. Our good-faith decisions on verification are final to the extent permitted
    by law.\r\n\r\n<b>8. Optional prize competition</b>\r\nThe competition begins
    on September 8, 2026, at 12:00 PM Eastern Time and ends on September 18, 2026,
    at 12:00 PM Eastern Time (\"Competition Period\"). Entries received outside the
    Competition Period are not eligible.\r\n\r\nTo enter, an eligible adult must
    enter their name and email address as requested through the game and play the
    game during the Competition Period. No purchase or payment is required.\r\n\r\nEach
    entrant may play an unlimited number of times during the Competition Period.
    However, the three lives described in section 6 apply within each play session.\r\n\r\nThere
    may be up to 35 potential winners.\r\n\r\nEach verified winner will receive a
    ManningCast Heist Gift Pack, with an estimated retail value of $500.\r\n\r\nAn
    entry is complete only when we receive the required name, email address, and
    eligible score. Entries must be truthful and complete. One person may not enter
    through multiple names or email addresses to evade an entry limit.\r\n\r\n<b>9.
    Ranking and ties</b>\r\nEligible entrants will be ranked from highest to lowest
    verified score. The entrant or entrants occupying the number of winning positions
    specified in section 8 will be potential winners, subject to verification of
    eligibility and compliance with these terms.\r\n\r\nIf two or more entrants have
    the same verified score at a winning position, the tie will be resolved in this
    order:\r\nthe faster verified completion time ranks higher;\r\nif still tied,
    the greater verified number of lives remaining ranks higher;\r\nif still tied,
    the greater verified number of points attributable to landing spaces ranks higher;
    and\r\nif still tied, the tied entrants will complete an additional skill-based
    play session under the same scoring conditions by a deadline we provide.\r\n\r\nNo
    tie will be resolved by a random drawing.\r\n\r\n<b>10. Potential winners and
    prizes</b>\r\nWe will contact each potential winner using the email address submitted
    with the entry. A potential winner must respond within 72 hours after the notice
    is sent and may be required to confirm eligibility and provide information reasonably
    necessary to deliver the prize and satisfy tax or legal requirements.\r\n\r\nIf
    a potential winner is ineligible, cannot be contacted, does not respond by the
    deadline, declines the prize, or does not provide required verification, the
    potential winner forfeits the prize. We may then offer the prize to the next
    highest-ranked eligible entrant, applying the tie procedures in section 9 if
    necessary.\r\n\r\nA winner may not transfer, substitute, or redeem a prize for
    cash. Omaha may substitute a prize of comparable or greater value. A winner is
    responsible for taxes and any expenses not expressly stated as part of the prize.
    Prizes are awarded \"as is\" with no warranty or guarantee, either express or
    implied.\r\n\r\nA potential winner is not a confirmed winner until we complete
    verification. Prizes will be delivered within 25 business days after verification,
    unless a different timing is stated in the prize description. All prize details
    are at Omaha's discretion.\r\n\r\nLimit one (1) prize per person.\r\n\r\n<b>11.
    Optional high-score publicity</b>\r\nAn eligible adult may separately choose
    whether to allow us to publicize their high-score achievement. This choice is
    voluntary, is not required to play or enter the prize competition, and does not
    affect scoring, ranking, or prize eligibility.\r\n\r\nIf you opt in, you allow
    us and our service providers to use your submitted name and score to identify
    and promote your high-score achievement in connection with the game and competition,
    without additional payment, where permitted by law. We will not use your email
    address publicly.\r\n\r\nYou may withdraw this permission for future uses by
    contacting <link=\"mailto:info@omahaproductions.com\"><color=#4A9EFF>info@omahaproductions.com</color></link>.
    A withdrawal does not require us to recall materials already published or distributed
    before we processed the withdrawal.\r\n\r\n<b>12. Optional competition and marketing
    communications</b>\r\nIf you enter the competition, we may use your email address
    to administer your entry, verify eligibility and scoring, notify you about winner
    status, deliver a prize, prevent fraud, and satisfy legal obligations. These
    administrative messages are part of the competition and are not marketing.\r\n\r\nMarketing
    communications are optional and require a separate affirmative choice. Declining
    marketing does not affect gameplay, scoring, competition entry, or prize eligibility.
    If you opt in, you may later unsubscribe using the method provided in the message
    or by contacting us.\r\n\r\n<b>13. Information and privacy</b>\r\nBecause there
    is no separate privacy notice, this section describes the information handled
    through the game and how we use and disclose it.\r\n\r\nIf you play without entering
    or selecting an optional choice, we may process technical and gameplay information
    such as device and browser information, internet protocol address, security and
    diagnostic data, game events, scores, completion time, remaining lives, and landing-space
    results. We use that information to provide and secure the game, calculate and
    verify scores, prevent fraud and abuse, troubleshoot problems, and comply with
    law.\r\n\r\nIf you enter the competition, we also collect your name and email
    address. If you make an optional publicity or marketing choice, we record that
    choice. For a potential winner, we may request additional information reasonably
    necessary to verify eligibility, deliver the prize, and satisfy tax or legal
    obligations.\r\n\r\nWe may disclose information to service providers that help
    us host, secure, maintain, analyze, or administer the game and competition; to
    professional advisers; to authorities or other parties when reasonably necessary
    to comply with law or protect rights, safety, or security; and as part of a merger,
    financing, reorganization, or sale of all or part of the relevant business. We
    do not authorize service providers to use the information for their own marketing.\r\n\r\nWe
    retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes
    described in these terms, including competition administration, security, dispute
    resolution, and legal compliance, and then delete or deidentify it when reasonably
    practicable.\r\n\r\nTo ask about information handled through the game, request
    correction or deletion where applicable, or withdraw an optional consent, contact
    us using the contact information provided in section 23 below. We will respond
    as required by applicable law and may need to verify the request.\r\n\r\n<b>14.
    Fair play</b>\r\nYou may not cheat, use bots or automated tools, manipulate gameplay
    or scoring, exploit an unintended error, interfere with another player, submit
    false information, impersonate another person, bypass an eligibility or entry
    limit, or disrupt the game or its security.\r\n\r\nWe may disqualify an entry,
    invalidate a score, restrict access, or take other reasonable action if we determine
    in good faith that a person acted in an unsportsmanlike or disruptive manner,
    violated these terms or compromised the integrity of the game or competition.
    All decisions made by us are final and binding.\r\n\r\n<b>15. Technical failures
    and competition integrity</b>\r\nWe are not responsible for lost, late, incomplete,
    damaged, inaccurate, stolen, delayed, misdirected, undelivered or garbled entries,
    scores, game play, emails, messages or other communications of any kind; or for
    lost, interrupted or unavailable network, server, Internet Service Provider (ISP),
    website, or other connections, availability or accessibility or miscommunications
    or failed computer, satellite, telephone or cable transmissions, lines, or technical
    failure or jumbled, scrambled, delayed, or misdirected transmissions or computer
    hardware or software malfunctions, failures or difficulties, or other errors
    or difficulties of any kind whether human, mechanical, electronic, computer,
    network, typographical, printing or otherwise relating to or in connection with
    the game or the competition, including, without limitation, errors or difficulties
    which may occur in connection with the administration of the game or competition,
    the processing of entries, scores, or game play, the announcement of the prizes,
    or in any game or competition-related materials. We are also not responsible
    for any incorrect or inaccurate information, whether caused by site users, tampering,
    hacking, or by any equipment or programming associated with or utilized in the
    game. We are not responsible for injury or damage to any person's computer or
    other device related to or resulting from participating in this game or competition
    or downloading materials from or use of any website. Persons who tamper with
    or abuse any aspect of the game or competition or website, who act in an unsportsmanlike
    or disruptive manner or who are in violation of these terms, as solely determined
    by Omaha, will be disqualified and all associated entries will be void. \n<b>CAUTION:
    ANY ATTEMPT TO DELIBERATELY DAMAGE OR UNDERMINE THE LEGITIMATE OPERATION OF THE
    GAME OR COMPETITION MAY BE IN VIOLATION OF CRIMINAL AND CIVIL LAWS AND SHOULD
    SUCH AN ATTEMPT BE MADE, WE RESERVE THE RIGHT TO SEEK DAMAGES AND OTHER REMEDIES
    (INCLUDING ATTORNEYS' FEES) FROM ANY SUCH INDIVIDUAL TO THE FULLEST EXTENT OF
    THE LAW, INCLUDING CRIMINAL PROSECUTION.</b>\r\n\r\nIf a technical, security,
    fraud, or legal issue materially affects the integrity or administration of the
    competition, we may pause, extend, modify, or cancel the affected portion to
    the extent reasonably necessary and permitted by law. When practicable, we will
    preserve verified eligible scores and apply a remedy that does not unfairly favor
    or disadvantage entrants.\r\n\r\n<b>16. Availability and changes to the game</b>\r\nWe
    may maintain, update, suspend, or discontinue all or part of the game. Availability
    may vary by device, browser, location, and time. Any change affecting an active
    competition remains subject to section 15 and will not retroactively change verified
    scoring or prize eligibility except as reasonably necessary to address an integrity
    issue and as permitted by law.\r\n\r\n<b>17. Disclaimers</b>\r\nTo the fullest
    extent permitted by law, the game and competition are provided \"as is\" and
    \"as available.\" We disclaim implied warranties, including merchantability,
    fitness for a particular purpose, title, and noninfringement. We do not promise
    uninterrupted or error-free operation or that the game will work with every device
    or browser.\r\n\r\nSome jurisdictions do not allow certain warranty exclusions,
    so some of the foregoing may not apply to you. Nothing in these terms excludes
    a right or remedy that cannot lawfully be excluded.\r\n\r\n<b>18. Limitation
    of liability</b>\r\nTo the fullest extent permitted by law, we and our affiliates,
    licensors, service providers, and their respective officers, directors, employees,
    and agents will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential,
    exemplary, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, data, goodwill, or opportunities,
    arising from or relating to the game or competition.\r\n\r\nTo the fullest extent
    permitted by law, our total aggregate liability arising from or relating to the
    game, competition, or these terms will not exceed the greater of $100 or the
    amount you paid us, if any, to use the game during the twelve months before the
    event giving rise to the claim.\r\n\r\nThe limitations in this section do not
    apply to liability that cannot lawfully be limited. Some jurisdictions do not
    allow certain limitations, so some of them may not apply to you.\r\n\r\n<b>19.
    Suspension and termination</b>\r\nWe may suspend or terminate your access, invalidate
    a score or entry, or disqualify you from the competition if we reasonably believe
    you violated these terms, created a security or legal risk, or compromised fair
    play. We may take proportionate steps to investigate and document the basis for
    that action.\r\n\r\nYou may stop using the game at any time. Provisions that
    by their nature should continue after access ends, including ownership, disclaimers,
    liability limitations, governing law, disputes, and general provisions, will
    survive.\r\n\r\n<b>20. Governing law and disputes</b>\r\nThese terms and any
    dispute arising from or relating to the game or competition are governed by the
    laws of the State of New York, without regard to conflict-of-law principles,
    except to the extent another law must apply and cannot lawfully be waived.\r\n\r\nBefore
    filing a claim, you and we will make a good-faith effort for 30 days to resolve
    it informally after one party gives the other written notice describing the dispute
    and requested relief.\r\n\r\nIf the dispute is not resolved, each party agrees
    to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts located in New
    York County, New York, except where applicable law gives you the right to bring
    a claim in another court. Each party waives objection to venue in those courts
    to the extent permitted by law.\r\n\r\n<b>21. Changes to these terms</b>\r\nWe
    may update these terms prospectively when reasonably necessary to address an
    operational change, technical or security issue, or legal requirement. The updated
    version will state its effective date and will be made available with the game.\r\n\r\nA
    material update will not retroactively change eligibility, scoring, ranking,
    or prizes for a competition already underway, except as reasonably necessary
    to preserve competition integrity and as permitted by law.\r\n\r\n<b>22. General
    provisions</b>\r\nIf a court finds part of these terms unenforceable, that part
    will be enforced to the maximum extent permitted and the remaining provisions
    will continue in effect. A failure to enforce a provision is not a waiver. You
    may not assign your rights or obligations under these terms without our written
    consent. We may assign these terms as part of a corporate transaction or transfer
    of the game, subject to applicable law.\r\n\r\n<b>23. Contact</b>\r\nQuestions
    about the game, competition, these terms, or information handled through the
    game may be sent to:\r\n\r\nOmaha Productions LLC\r\n11601 Wilshire Boulevard\r\nLos
    Angeles, CA 90025\r\n<link=\"mailto:info@omahaproductions.com\"><color=#4A9EFF>info@omahaproductions.com</color></link>\r\n\r\n<b>24.
